      "that_understands_fire_water_and_wildli": " that understands fire, water, and wildlife as interconnected systems. Restoring all three together — not just one in isolation — is the most effective strategy for building landscape resilience in an era of increasing wildfire risk.",
      "the_basketry_tree_annual_growth_rings_": "The basketry tree. Annual growth rings split into splints when the trunk is pounded.",
      "the_bilingual_terms_across_this_sim_th": "The bilingual terms across this sim. The Wabanaki Confederacy is five distinct nations (Penobscot, Passamaquoddy, Maliseet, Mi'kmaq, Abenaki), each with its own language. Spellings vary by orthography and dialect; the forms here are representative, not authoritative. For language teaching consult the language program of each nation, the University of Maine Wabanaki Center, or community resources directly.",
      "the_fire_triangle_fuel_oxygen_heat_com": "The fire triangle: fuel + oxygen + heat. Combustion is exothermic oxidation. Flashover = the moment ambient air reaches ignition temperature — catastrophic.",
