      "essential_fatty_acids": "Essential Fatty Acids",
      "even_at_rest_muscles_maintain_tone_and": "Even at rest, muscles maintain tone and run baseline metabolism.",
      "even_when_you_re_resting_your_body_use": "Even when you're resting, your body uses energy. The minimum to keep your heart beating, brain firing, lungs breathing, kidneys filtering, and core temperature stable is called Basal Metabolic Rate (BMR). Most adolescents have a BMR somewhere between 1,200 and 1,800 kcal/day — the wide range is normal biological variation.",
      "every_cell_holds_50g_of_atp_and_recycl": "Every cell holds ~50g of ATP and recycles it ~1,000× per day.",
      "every_cell_in_your_body_runs_on_a_tiny": "Every cell in your body runs on a tiny molecule called ATP (adenosine triphosphate). When ATP gives up one phosphate group, it becomes ADP and releases energy your cells use to do work — contract muscles, fire neurons, build proteins, push molecules across membranes.",
      "every_major_platform_has_a_category_fo": "Every major platform has a category for this. Reporting is anonymous; the creator doesn't see you reported them. NEDA tracks platform responses and pushes for stronger moderation.",
